.TH XYMONTOOLS 1 "Version 4.3.30:  4 Sep 2019" "Xymon"
.SH NAME
xymontools, xymonloadhosts, xymonstackio, xymonavailability, xymonlocator, xymonnetprobe \- Xymon diagnostic tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "xymonloadhosts HOSTSFILE HOSTNAME [HOSTNAME...]"
.br
.B "xymonloadhosts @ HOSTNAME"
.br
.B "xymonstackio FILENAME"
.br
.B "xymonavailability HISTFILE STARTTIME ENDTIME"
.br
.B "xymonlocator IP:PORT"
.br
.B "xymonnetprobe [--debug] [--timeout=N] [--concurrency=N] IP/PORT/TESTSPEC[@SOURCEIP]..."

.SH DESCRIPTION
These programs run one piece of the Xymon server by hand, using the
same code as the daemons, to show what that piece makes of a
configuration file, a history file or a network service. They are
installed only by "make install-tools", not by "make install".

Each one prints its usage with \fB--help\fR. Run them under
.I xymoncmd(1)
so that they find the server's configuration.

.IP "\fBxymonloadhosts\fR"
Loads HOSTSFILE the way the server does, including its "include"
and "directory" lines, and prints every item of each HOSTNAME's
entry, after resolving the name to its canonical host. With "@"
it shows the entry xymond holds for HOSTNAME instead. It then
prompts: an item name prints that item, an empty line moves on to
the next host.
   xymonloadhosts /etc/xymon/hosts.cfg www.example.com

.IP "\fBxymonstackio\fR"
Prints FILENAME with its "include" and "directory" lines expanded,
then prompts: "?" lists every file that was read and whether any
of them changed since \- the check the server makes before it
reloads a configuration \- "!" reads it again and "." quits.
To print the expanded file only, use
.I xymoncfg(1).

.IP "\fBxymonavailability\fR"
Computes the availability of one status over a period, as the
report pages do, and lists the color changes in that period.
HISTFILE is a file in the history directory ($XYMONHISTDIR),
named HOST.SERVICE with the dots in HOST written as commas.
STARTTIME and ENDTIME are in Unix epoch format, as printed by
"date +%s".
   xymonavailability $XYMONHISTDIR/www,example,com.http 1700000000 1700086400

.IP "\fBxymonlocator\fR"
Connects to the
.I xymond_locator
at IP:PORT and prompts for its commands. Its register, down, up
and forget commands change the state of that running locator.

.IP "\fBxymonnetprobe\fR"
Runs each network test once, the way
.I xymonnet(1)
does, and prints the result, including the banner the service
sent. TESTSPEC is a service from protocols.cfg. --debug adds a
trace of each step.
   xymonnetprobe --debug 172.16.10.2/25/smtp

.SH "SEE ALSO"
xymoncmd(1), xymoncfg(1), xymongrep(1), xymonnet(1), hosts.cfg(5), xymon(7)
